# Ledger row #1 — I/O, L1 — per-worker decoded-sample cache
# File: pecan/dataset.py, Dataset_PDB.__getitem__
# Verdict: KEPT — the real measured win (-8.5% wall time, isolated via
# PECAN_DECODE_CACHE=0 A/B, 2 replicates, CV 0.65%)
#
# Mechanism: caches the fully-decoded (coord, feat) arrays per (pdbid,poseid)
# after first read, so epoch 2+ skips the h5py dataset read entirely for a
# repeated sample. Guarded OFF for modality==1 (point cloud), which applies a
# fresh random affine augmentation to coord on every __getitem__ call — caching
# would freeze the augmentation across epochs. modality==3 (graph
# representation, the active config in this session) has no per-sample
# augmentation, so caching there is correctness-safe.

